          caption: "A newly dilated, unreactive pupil on one side is the third nerve being crushed against the tentorium by a herniating temporal lobe: call the doctor and the neurosurgeon, secure the airway, give mannitol or hypertonic saline, and move towards the scanner. It is a sign that should rarely be reached, because the conscious level changed first.",
